{"name":"Weekend Gardener","hex":"#9fe4aa","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"weekend","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The break in the working week, usually two days including the traditional holy or sabbath day. Thus in Western countries, Saturday and Sunday."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spend the weekend."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weekend"},{"term":"gardener","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who gardens; one who grows plants or cultivates a garden.","A coachman who drives badly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gardener"}],"entries":[{"title":"Workweek and weekend","blocks":[{"text":"The weekdays and weekend are the complementary parts of the week, devoted to labour and rest, respectively. The legal weekdays, or workweek, is the part of the seven-day week devoted to working. In most of the world, the workweek is from Monday to Friday and the weekend is Saturday and Sunday. A weekday or workday is any day of the working week. Other institutions often follow this pattern, such as places of education. The constituted weekend has varying definitions, based on determined calendar days, designated period of time, and/or regional definition of the working week. Sometimes the term \"weekend\" is expanded to include the time after work hours on the last workday of the week.\nWeekdays and workdays can be further detailed in terms of working time, the period of time that an individual spends at paid occupational labor."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Workweek_and_weekend"},{"title":"Gardener","blocks":[{"text":"A gardener is someone who practices gardening, either professionally or as a hobby."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Abel_Grimmer_-_Spring_-_WGA10683.jpg/330px-Abel_Grimmer_-_Spring_-_WGA10683.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gardener"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Almost_empty_calendar.JPG/500px-Almost_empty_calendar.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Almost_empty_calendar.JPG/1280px-Almost_empty_calendar.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Almost_empty_calendar.JPG/500px-Almost_empty_calendar.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This day planner chart (which can be used for any months) shows the workweek days as white boxes and the weekend days as light blue-coloured boxes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlmost_empty_calendar.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Gardening.jpg/500px-Gardening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Gardening.jpg/1280px-Gardening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Gardening.jpg/500px-Gardening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A gardener","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGardening.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Royal_Gardener_John_Rose_and_King_Charles_II_-_Hendrick_Danckerts_1675.jpeg/500px-Royal_Gardener_John_Rose_and_King_Charles_II_-_Hendrick_Danckerts_1675.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Royal_Gardener_John_Rose_and_King_Charles_II_-_Hendrick_Danckerts_1675.jpeg/500px-Royal_Gardener_John_Rose_and_King_Charles_II_-_Hendrick_Danckerts_1675.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","